 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for browser delivery.** Delivery maintains direct browser sessions and uses revision replay for recovery. Five-second HTTPS polling was rejected because its repeated reads and delivery lag work against fast board updates. A hosted realtime service was rejected because the board should not depend on a realtime vendor when the team accepts responsibility for connection capacity and reconnect operations.
